import Fresh.SelectRung1Data

/-!
# PerWalkHdom: the per-walk CapsDom attestation instances for box b1 (Track C data layer)

New file (2026-11-21); nothing existing is edited; generated by
`experiments/n8/onefast_audit/perwalkhdom_gen_v1.py` from the verified per-walk data
(`perwalk_v2_census.jsonl` + `perwalk_v2_traces.jsonl`, E911).

Walk key: the `perwalk_v2_words.jsonl` enumeration index (phase1's DFS yield order,
the enumeration of record -- phase1 asserts a yield-prefix on every resume).  The
trace/census lines are joined BY WORD IDENTITY: the JSONL `seq` fields carry
run-local orderings (an aborted early run left 20 mislabeled lines, and the phase2/3
indexing differs from the final words-file order), so this generator joins on the
word -- each of the 804 words appears exactly once in each file -- and re-keys by the
words-file index.  All E911 statistics (804/804 attested, the 564 census-trace TabLe
failures, the 3+6 distinct pair values, the 8 pair-value combos, the equality counts)
were re-verified under this canonical indexing before emission.

## The datum and its provenance

The select rung `Fresh.SelectRung1.selectRung1_1_3_4_5_5_5_7` needs, per realized
first-window walk, a record of `compFamOf b1` attesting FROM THAT WALK
(`AttestsFrom e walk U`).  Its banked form demanded the walk's trace be `TabLe`-below
the ONE census trace `T8_1_3_4_5_5_5_7_12` (all 49 pairs); that uniform `hdom` is
REFUTED as a box-uniform datum
(`Fresh.SelectRung1Data.selectRung1_hdom_owed_unsupplyable_b1`, walk19 at pair (0,1)).
The route decision therefore forces the PER-WALK form, and `perwalk_v2` (E911) verified
its data layer: for EVERY one of the 804 realized first-window walks W of the closure
start `mkTab_1_3_4_5_5_5_7` (lengths 18..28; the class coincides, as a set, with the
dump's table-level 804-word enumeration), ALL FOUR records r0..r3 of
`compFam_1_3_4_5_5_5_7` attest W's OWN endpoint trace: `CapsDom V_W e.y e.caps e.x`.

The reconciliation: `CapsDom` reads only the pairs of the record's cap walk -- the
trace-relevant pairs, mechanically the union of the four records' cap pairs, is
{(0,6), (1,6)}.  The 564 census-trace `TabLe` failures live on 12 OTHER pairs and
never touch these two on any walk: on every walk the stored entry at (0,6) is one of
3 distinct values, all ≤ 1870/13113 (max with equality on 36 walks), and the entry at
(1,6) is one of 6 distinct values, all ≤ 55/117 (max with equality on 240 walks).

## What is banked (and the honest scope)

Per walk W (seq n), a literal relevant-pair trace projection `VWalk_n : UTable`: the
two stored pairs with their exact trace values and strict flags, `none` elsewhere.
`CapsDom` treats `none` as the loosest bound and reads only the cap pairs, so the
projection is EXACTLY what the attestation consumes; the full 49-pair traces stay in
`perwalk_v2_traces.jsonl`.  Per walk, the instance theorem

    hdom_walk_n : CapsDom VWalk_n (0 : Fin 7) [(6, (1870/13113 : ℝ))] (6 : Fin 7) ∧
                  CapsDom VWalk_n (1 : Fin 7) [(6, (55/117 : ℝ))] (6 : Fin 7)

(r0 = ⟨6, 0, 13, 3, [(6, 1870/13113)]⟩ and r1 = ⟨6, 1, 65, 31, [(6, 55/117)]⟩; r2/r3
share r1's pair and cap, so these two conjuncts carry all four records' conditions).
Each proof is `capsDom_single` on an inline `rfl` entry and an inline `norm_num`
comparison (the `Fresh.BandCertDataExt` per-instance pattern).  The enumeration
`walkInstances` (804 (seq, len, table) triples, perwalk_v2 order) carries the class as
data, and `hdom_perwalk_b1` states the aggregate in the select shape: every banked
instance carries SOME record of `compFamOf b1` attesting its own projection at the
record's cap pair.

All arithmetic is exact (`rfl` on the literal entries; `norm_num` on the emitted
comparisons; data-side this generator asserts the same inequalities in `Fraction` and
reproduces the deepest walk's trace through the value-verbatim `l_`-mirror).  Every
theorem carries `#print axioms`; the accepted profile is the standard three --
`sorryAx` is failure.
-/

namespace Fresh.PerWalkHdom

open Fresh.ChainDomBase Fresh.CapChainsOfCarve Fresh.JoinFamComposed Fresh.OneSidedComposed
  Fresh.OneSidedGlue Fresh.UClosure Fresh.SpineSound Fresh.FilterAssembly Fresh.DumpDomData
